<?jelly escape-by-default='true'?>
<j:jelly xmlns:j="jelly:core">
  <div class="jenkins-alert jenkins-alert-warning">
    <p>Controllers of this cluster saved the same setting at the same moment, and the later save overwrote the other
      (conflict policy <code>${it.policy}</code>). Changes to different settings were merged.
      To refuse such saves made in the UI instead (the user then reloads and saves again), start the controllers with
      <code>-Djenkins.persistence.PersistenceStores.conflicts=strict-ui</code>.</p>
    <table class="jenkins-table jenkins-table--small">
      <thead><tr><th>Controller</th><th>Merged</th><th>Overwritten</th><th>Refused</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <j:forEach var="c" items="${it.counts}">
          <tr><td>${c.controller()}</td><td>${c.merged()}</td><td>${c.overwritten()}</td><td>${c.refused()}</td></tr>
        </j:forEach>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</j:jelly>
